}],"mentions":[{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":170,"text":"…jalonado por maravillosas pildoras refrescantes como «Got to Get» de Rob’N’Raz con Leila K, «It’s on You» de MC Sar & The Real McCoy, «The Power» de Snap!, «Keep on Tryin’» de Twenty 4 Seven, «Helio Afrika» de Dr. Alban, «No Limit» y «Get Ready for This» de 2 Unlimited, «Mr. Vain» de Culture Beat, «The…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Frankfurt Production Duo","body":"Snap! comprised two producers from Frankfurt, Germany, who originated from the city's EBM and Newbeat scenes. They applied their background in electronic music to develop the Eurodance sound. \"Con un lado Snap eran dos productores de Frankfurt que venían de la escena Ebime y el Newbeet.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"La gran mentira detrás del Eurodance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_F34L8wfrdo"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Producer-Rapper Formula","body":"Snap! was a pioneer in establishing a standard Eurodance formula where producers, needing charisma for television, recruited rappers. These rappers, often American ex-military personnel found in clubs, were signed for low fees to front the act, providing a touch of \"American credibility\" to the music for broader appeal. \"Snap eran dos productores de Frankfurt que venían de la escena Ebime y el Newbeet. [...] necesitaban el carisma de una estrella, así que las crearon.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"La gran mentira detrás del Eurodance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_F34L8wfrdo"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":92371359273039,"type":"song","name":"The Power","work_year":1990,"list_id":83116008556051,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1990","src":"singles","rank":26,"year":1990,"note":"","yt":"nm6DO_7px1I","scaruffi":null},{"id":92371359273039,"type":"song","name":"The Power","work_year":1990,"